<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hyundai to export 30,000 buses to Iran.</title>
<headline>Hyundai to export 30,000 buses to Iran.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hyundai Motor Co Ltd, South Korea's largest carmaker, said on Monday it would export 30,000 mid-sized buses to Iran over the next 10 years.</p>
<p>A Hyundai spokesman said Hyundai signed the export contract with Iran Khodro Co on June 29, under which 3,000 semi-finished Chorus buses would be shipped to Iran annually.</p>
<p>Production facilities would also be transferred to the Iranian company to complete the bus assembly, Hyundai said.</p>
</text>
